wg-augment-cyber-arm = Cybernetic arm
wg-augment-cyber-arm-desc = A plain cybernetic arm and hand. Works like the real thing, and patches up with a welder and some cable. Doesn't like EMPs.
wg-augment-cyber-leg = Cybernetic leg
wg-augment-cyber-leg-desc = A plain cybernetic leg and foot. Works like the real thing, and patches up with a welder and some cable. Doesn't like EMPs.

wg-augment-mantis-blade-left = Mantis blade
wg-augment-mantis-blade-right = Mantis blade
wg-augment-mantis-blade-desc = A blade folded along the forearm that snaps out on command. They won't see the steel until it's too late. Needs a cybernetic arm.
wg-augment-dermal-armor = E-SAPI dermal armor
wg-augment-dermal-armor-desc = Vanguard armor plates set under the skin. Bullets and blades bite less, but heat and shock hurt more.
wg-augment-muscle-fibers = Muscle fiber suite
wg-augment-muscle-fibers-desc = Reinforced muscle fibers that let you dash a short way in a pinch.
wg-augment-tool-arm = PD-VI RM-5 "Verstak" tool arm
wg-augment-tool-arm-desc = A Vanguard engineer's forearm. A screwdriver, wrench, welder, crowbar, wirecutters and multitool fold out one at a time from a wheel, and the welder refills every time it goes away. An EMP locks it shut until it wears off. Needs a cybernetic arm.
wg-augment-smartlink = MMC SL-4 "Shojun" smartlink
wg-augment-smartlink-desc = Mieyo's answer to recoil. The hand talks to the gun it holds, so the gun barely kicks, its spread builds up slower and settles faster, and its rounds leave the barrel faster. Your eyes mark the closest target to your aim and count the rounds left. An EMP shuts the hand down, and it drops whatever it's holding. Needs a cybernetic hand.
wg-smartlink-ammo = {$count}/{$capacity}
wg-smartlink-range = {$meters}m
wg-augment-halo-burst = TSF KR-30 "Corona" frag charges
wg-augment-halo-burst-desc = Marine Corps breaching kit: frag charges packed around the ribcage. Throws a ring of charges out around you that go off two seconds later, tearing into anyone close, friends included, and knocking them back. You're held in place behind a shield until they blow. Holds two charges, and each comes back after three minutes.
wg-augment-halo-stun = TSF KR-31 "Corona" concussion charges
wg-augment-halo-stun-desc = The Marine Corps' less-lethal option: concussion charges packed around the ribcage. Throws a ring of charges out around you that go off two seconds later, knocking the wind out of anyone close, friends included, and knocking them back. You're held in place behind a shield until they blow. Holds two charges, and each comes back after three minutes.
wg-burst-launcher-recharged = Corona charge ready ({ $charges }/{ $max }).
wg-augment-thermal-tint-eyes = PD-VI OV-40 "Tapetum" ocular suite
wg-augment-thermal-tint-eyes-desc = Vanguard scout optics. One button runs through thermal, which picks out body heat through walls, then green, cyan and white night vision. They block welding glare, but a flash still blinds you.
wg-augment-finger-lighter = MMC HB-2 "Hibana" finger lighter
wg-augment-finger-lighter-desc = A lighter in your fingertip, for people who never have one on them. An EMP snuffs it out for a while.
wg-augment-deployable-emp = The implant doesn't respond.
wg-augment-deployable-stow = Stow the {$item}
wg-augment-arm-laser = MMC HT-6 "Hotaru" arm laser
wg-augment-arm-laser-desc = Mieyo close protection: a laser emitter that slides out of the forearm into your hand. It fires as fast as you can pull the trigger, but each shot is weak, and the cell in the arm runs dry after about twenty-five. With one in each arm, both fire together, but wilder. The cell recharges on its own, out or folded away, once you stop firing. An EMP locks it shut until it wears off. Needs a cybernetic arm.
wg-augment-hand-shield = PD-VI ZS-3 "Zaslon" hand shield
wg-augment-hand-shield-desc = A Vanguard breacher's shield, projected from the palm. Raised, it fills that hand, slows you a little and stops bullets, blows and bolts from the front, turning lasers aside. Every hit drains it, and it only recharges while lowered. Drain it completely and it collapses, and it won't come back up until it's full again. You can only have one. Needs a cybernetic hand.
wg-augment-optical-camo = MMC KG-9 "Kasumi" optical camouflage
wg-augment-optical-camo-desc = Light-bending cells under the skin. For twenty seconds, stand still and you're gone; move and you shimmer back into sight, fading again once you stop. Attacking, shooting or getting hurt drops it, and it needs a minute to come back. An EMP knocks it out for two.
wg-augment-shoulder-cannon = TSF KR-40 "Grom" shoulder cannon
wg-augment-shoulder-cannon-desc = A Marine Corps plasma cannon on an arm behind the shoulder, leaving your hands free. Swing it up over your shoulder and middle-click a spot; after a short charge it throws a heavy plasma bolt there. Anyone can see it raised. The bolt is slower than a bullet, so it can be dodged from far away. Reloads in five seconds, and an EMP folds it away and locks it for a minute. Needs a cybernetic chest.
wg-shoulder-cannon-cooling = The cannon is still cooling down.
wg-hand-shield-collapse = Your shield flickers out!
wg-hand-shield-recharging = Your shield is still recharging.
wg-hand-shield-other = Your other shield is already up.
wg-optical-camo-off = You shimmer back into view.
wg-optical-camo-blocked = Your camouflage won't start while something else is hiding you.
wg-augment-adrenal-booster = TSF KR-14 "Ryvok" adrenal booster
wg-augment-adrenal-booster-desc = Marine Corps combat booster on the adrenal glands. More stamina, and it comes back faster. When a stun puts you down, it floods you with adrenaline and you're back on your feet a moment later; after that it needs two minutes to recover. Adrenaline from pain lasts twice as long. Won't fit in a cybernetic chest.
wg-adrenal-booster-surge = Adrenaline floods you, and you push yourself back up!
wg-adrenal-booster-surge-others = { CAPITALIZE(THE($target)) } shakes it off and gets back up!
wg-adrenal-booster-ready = Your adrenal booster has recovered.
wg-augment-pain-editor = MMC EVT-130 "Mushin" pain inhibitor
wg-augment-pain-editor-desc = A Mieyo filter on the brainstem, sold to people who can't afford to stop working. Every wound hurts less, so it takes more to put you down.
wg-augment-reflex-booster = PD-VI NR-8 "Strizh" reflex booster
wg-augment-reflex-booster-desc = Vanguard pilots swear by it. Ships you fly accelerate and turn 15% better, and about one bullet in twenty that should have hit you misses. Your nerves run hot, so wounds hurt a little more. Does nothing against lasers.
wg-reflex-booster-dodge = { CAPITALIZE(THE($target)) } twists out of the way!

wg-augment-cyber-chest = PD-VI KS-2 "Kiras" chest chassis
wg-augment-cyber-chest-desc = Your chest rebuilt around a Vanguard combat frame, in a style of your choice. Room for three implants instead of two, but implants that need living tissue won't fit.

wg-augment-holo-projector = MMC KG-7 "Kagemusha" holo projector
wg-augment-holo-projector-desc = Mieyo executive protection. Emitters under the skin cast two copies of you around the room, and you swap places with one of them. The copies wander for twenty seconds, give off no heat and vanish when hit. Won't cast in a doorway or a tight spot, and never past a wall or door. Recharges in ninety seconds.
wg-holo-projector-cramped = There's no room here to cast your copies.
wg-augment-threat-sole = PD-VI SP-9 "Sapyor" sole sensors
wg-augment-threat-sole-desc = Vanguard sapper sensors in the sole of the foot. Mines, tripwires and other floor traps don't go off under you. One foot is enough. In a cybernetic foot, an EMP knocks them out along with the foot.
wg-augment-nutriment-pump = PD-VI PN-3 "Paek" nutriment pump
wg-augment-nutriment-pump-desc = A ration pump beside the stomach, standard issue on long Vanguard patrols. It won't let you starve, but it won't stop you being hungry either. Won't fit in a cybernetic chest.
wg-augment-nutriment-pump-feed = You feel less hungry...
wg-augment-reviver = MMC EVT-090 "Fukkatsu" cardiac reviver
wg-augment-reviver-desc = Mieyo's idea of a health plan: a defibrillator wired straight to the heart. When your heart stops, it holds your bleeding, tops up your blood and shocks you, up to three times, with the same odds as a medic's paddles. It won't close your wounds. It takes ten minutes to recharge afterwards, and an EMP knocks it out for two. Won't fit in a cybernetic chest.
wg-augment-reviver-charging = Something in your chest whines as it charges.
wg-augment-reviver-shock = { CAPITALIZE(THE($target)) } jolts as something in { POSS-ADJ($target) } chest fires!
wg-augment-iatric-monitor = MMC EVT-120 "Kanshi" vitals monitor
wg-augment-iatric-monitor-desc = A readout behind the eye that shows you your own vitals, like a health analyzer pointed at yourself.

